{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_e4ca8f895051410884c8b4bd","type":"tool_result","content":"I can't reproduce those methods verbatim — the full text of each far exceeds the strict 125-character limit I must apply to quoted material from a source document. Here's a concise rundown instead, based only on the page content (this file appears to be the `RealtimeSession` implementation from the MIT-licensed OpenAI Agents SDK, so you can pull the exact code from that project's repo):\n\n**`__init__`**\n- Stores the model, agent, a `RunContextWrapper`, event info, and history list; merges run-config and initial model settings into `_base_model_settings`.\n- Creates an unbounded asyncio event queue and initializes many state dicts/sets: pending tool calls, tool invocation routes, active invocations, pending outputs, and the dispatch snapshot.\n- Sets up guardrail bookkeeping: interrupted response IDs, per-item transcripts and run counts, response generation/ID/agent tracking, and a debounce length (default 100 via `guardrails_settings`).\n- Initializes guardrail and tool-call task sets and reads `async_tool_calls` from run config (defaulting to `True`).\n\n**`close`**\n- Returns early (after waking iterators) if already closed.\n- Raises `asyncio.CancelledError` if invoked from inside a tracked guardrail/tool-call task while cleanup is already running, to avoid a cycle.\n- Otherwise creates a cleanup task (named `\"agents-realtime-session-cleanup\"`) with a done callback, then awaits it via `asyncio.shield`.\n\n**`on_event`** (async)\n- Bails out if closing/closed; first queues a `RealtimeRawModelEvent`, then re-checks state.\n- Dispatches by `event.type`: errors, `function_call` (routed to a background task or inline handling depending on `_async_tool_calls`, with special redacted-error handling), audio, audio interrupted/done, transcription completed (history update plus added/updated events), timeout triggered, transcript and output-text deltas (feeding guardrail recording), item updated (with transcript-merge preservation logic), item deleted, no-ops for connection status/other/raw server events, end-of-stream, turn started/ended (agent start/end events plus guardrail lifecycle cleanup), usage accumulation, and stored exceptions; unknown types hit `assert_never`.\n\n**`_handle_tool_call`** (async)\n- Resolves the agent and dispatch snapshot, validates against call-ID reuse and duplicate/already-executed invocations via identity and status checks, then begins the tool call.\n- Flushes any pending output; otherwise resolves/filters the snapshot and routes by name: function tools (approval flow, pre-execution input guardrails, a start event, invocation, output completion), handoffs (invoke handoff, swap the current agent, send updated settings with the transfer message), or unknown tools (error output plus a `RealtimeError`).\n- Wrapped in try/finally so `_finish_tool_call` always runs.\n\n**`_get_new_history`** (decorated with `@classmethod`)\n- For transcription-completed events, merges the transcript into matching user audio items or appends a new user message.\n- For items: updates existing entries in place — replacing non-message items, merging assistant/user/system message content while preserving non-empty transcripts, text, and images — otherwise inserting after `previous_item_id` if present, or appending at the end."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"13d715a6-efdd-4627-ab02-a32241b860a9","uuid":"2665579c-6bee-48f0-9f3a-1bf932a15bc5","timestamp":"2026-09-04T06:05:05.193Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":86676,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"I can't reproduce those methods verbatim — the full text of each far exceeds the strict 125-character limit I must apply to quoted material from a source document. Here's a concise rundown instead, based only on the page content (this file appears to be the `RealtimeSession` implementation from the MIT-licensed OpenAI Agents SDK, so you can pull the exact code from that project's repo):\n\n**`__init__`**\n- Stores the model, agent, a `RunContextWrapper`, event info, and history list; merges run-config and initial model settings into `_base_model_settings`.\n- Creates an unbounded asyncio event queue and initializes many state dicts/sets: pending tool calls, tool invocation routes, active invocations, pending outputs, and the dispatch snapshot.\n- Sets up guardrail bookkeeping: interrupted response IDs, per-item transcripts and run counts, response generation/ID/agent tracking, and a debounce length (default 100 via `guardrails_settings`).\n- Initializes guardrail and tool-call task sets and reads `async_tool_calls` from run config (defaulting to `True`).\n\n**`close`**\n- Returns early (after waking iterators) if already closed.\n- Raises `asyncio.CancelledError` if invoked from inside a tracked guardrail/tool-call task while cleanup is already running, to avoid a cycle.\n- Otherwise creates a cleanup task (named `\"agents-realtime-session-cleanup\"`) with a done callback, then awaits it via `asyncio.shield`.\n\n**`on_event`** (async)\n- Bails out if closing/closed; first queues a `RealtimeRawModelEvent`, then re-checks state.\n- Dispatches by `event.type`: errors, `function_call` (routed to a background task or inline handling depending on `_async_tool_calls`, with special redacted-error handling), audio, audio interrupted/done, transcription completed (history update plus added/updated events), timeout triggered, transcript and output-text deltas (feeding guardrail recording), item updated (with transcript-merge preservation logic), item deleted, no-ops for connection status/other/raw server events, end-of-stream, turn started/ended (agent start/end events plus guardrail lifecycle cleanup), usage accumulation, and stored exceptions; unknown types hit `assert_never`.\n\n**`_handle_tool_call`** (async)\n- Resolves the agent and dispatch snapshot, validates against call-ID reuse and duplicate/already-executed invocations via identity and status checks, then begins the tool call.\n- Flushes any pending output; otherwise resolves/filters the snapshot and routes by name: function tools (approval flow, pre-execution input guardrails, a start event, invocation, output completion), handoffs (invoke handoff, swap the current agent, send updated settings with the transfer message), or unknown tools (error output plus a `RealtimeError`).\n- Wrapped in try/finally so `_finish_tool_call` always runs.\n\n**`_get_new_history`** (decorated with `@classmethod`)\n- For transcription-completed events, merges the transcript into matching user audio items or appends a new user message.\n- For items: updates existing entries in place — replacing non-message items, merging assistant/user/system message content while preserving non-empty transcripts, text, and images — otherwise inserting after `previous_item_id` if present, or appending at the end.","durationMs":63740,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/openai/openai-agents-python/main/src/agents/realtime/session.py"}}
