{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788502237-e3ic5nXouhAVlB66mbrU","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The next commit after c0974d7c is `7a00eddd4a` — \"Tests for realtime session (#1080)\". That's a tests-only commit probably. Then `aab7bdd30b` \"Add tests for openai realtime model (#1081)\". Then `eafd8df998` (openai package upgrade). Then `a4499d4b72` guardrails, then `741da67b63` tracing.\n\nHmm — the user's task describes changes to session.py: removing background task handling, classmethod history update, close() without task cancellation. That's not a test-only commit. Let me check 7a00eddd4a (\"Tests for realtime session (#1080)\") — maybe it modified session.py too? The commit list for session.py didn't include it (page 2 started at a4499d4 and went forward). Actually wait, page 2's list ended with \"a4499d4 — Realtime guardrail support (#1082)\" as the last item, meaning there are no session.py commits between c0974d7c and a4499d4 other than a4499d4 itself... but hold on, that means the removal of `_background_task` happened in a4499d4's parent (741da67b \"Realtime tracing (#1084)\")? No wait — the sapling footer said #1082 stacks on #1084, but the actual git parent might differ.\n\nHmm wait, actually let me re-check. The a4499d4 diff for session.py didn't show `_background_task` in context. But git diffs only show ~3 lines of context. Let's look at the hunk:\n\n```\n@@ -79,9 +81,18 @@ def __init__(\n         self._event_info = RealtimeEventInfo(context=self._context_wrapper)\n         self._history: list[RealtimeItem] = []\n         self._model_config = model_config or {}\n+        self._run_config = run_config or {}\n         self._event_queue: asyncio.Queue[RealtimeSessionEvent] = asyncio.Queue()\n         self._closed = False\n \n+        # Guardrails state tracking\n```\n\nThe context shows `self._closed = False` followed by a blank line, then (end of hunk context). So in the parent of