ge 1 started at 4f7c1d66 (newest). So between a4499d4 and the newest, there are the page-1 commits; between c0974d7c and a4499d4, NO commits touched session.py. Interesting!\n\nSo the parent of a4499d4 (which is 741da67b \"Realtime tracing (#1084)\" or eafd8df998) must have had `_background_task` already removed... but no commit between c0974d7c and a4499d4 touched session.py. Contradiction?\n\nUnless... the parent chain: c0974d7c → 7a00eddd (Tests for realtime session #1080) → aab7bdd (tests for openai realtime model #1081) → eafd8df (fix openai package) → a4499d4 (guardrails #1082) → 741da67 (tracing #1084).\n\nHmm wait, but that ordering by date might not reflect actual git parentage (Sapling stack merges). The sapling footer in a4499d4 said \"#1084 → #1082\" meaning in the stack, #1084 comes BEFORE #1082. So a4499d4's parent is likely 741da67b (Realtime tracing #1084)?? But 741da67b has a later timestamp (17:09:56 vs 17:08:28). Hmm, the timestamps are close; the stack might have been landed in order #1084 then #1082? That seems odd but the footer says the stack is #1084 → #1082, and 741da67b is dated 1 minute later. Actually wait, if #1084 is the base of the stack and #1082 is stacked on top, then landing order would be #1084 first (741da67b at 17:09:56), then #1082 (a4499d4 at 17:08:28)? The dates are confusing because these are probably the dates Sapling created them, not landing order.\n\nAnyway, the key question: which commit removed `_background_task` and made `_get_new_history` a classmethod? Since no commit between c0974d7c and a4499d4 touched session.py per the path-filtered list... but wait, maybe the path-filtered list pagination missed some. Page 2 ended with a4499d4 and said \"21 commits total\". Page 1 had 22 entries? The page-1 list was truncated mid-list. Let me count page 1: it showed 23 entries (4f7c1d66 ... cc299884) and was truncated. So page 1 has more entries after cc299884. The boundary between page 1 and page 2 might skip commits! Page 1 truncated mid-list means I didn't see all of page 1 — the commits between cc299884 (2026-05-09) and a4499d4 (2025-07-12) are missing from my view.\n\nLet me get page 1 fully or use a different approach: fetch the commits list with until=a4499d4 to see commits before it touching session.py, i.e., the parent version. Actually more directly: I want to find the commit that changed session.py from the c0974d7c version (with _background_task) to a version without it.\n\nLet me look at commit 741da67b63 \"Realtime tracing (#1084)\" — its diff for session.py. If #1084 stacks on #1080-ish and includes the tool-call inline change... Actually, the tracing commit is large probably.\n\nAlternatively, let me directly check the parent of a4499d4: `git`-wise, I can fetch the commit object and see its parents.","signature":""}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Z.AI","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"13d715a6-efdd-4627-ab02-a32241b860a9","uuid":"7781849c-283a-460c-8bc2-a3ce9f35d77f","timestamp":"2026-09-04T06:11:31.066Z","request_id":"gen-1788502237-e3ic5nXouhAVlB66mbrU"}
