{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788502773-E97WrdFUTMlRBKHtWAtT","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"All done. The working tree now contains exactly the requested changes to `src/agents/realtime/session.py` (nothing else modified).\n\n## What changed\n\n**1. Tool calls handled inline — no background tasks** (`session.py:147`)\n```python\nelif event.type == \"function_call\":\n    await self._handle_tool_call(event)\n```\nThe `asyncio.create_task(...)` dispatch is gone; tool calls now run synchronously within `on_event`, so a failing tool's exception propagates to the event-processing flow instead of dying silently in a task. The `self._background_task` field was removed from `__init__`.\n\n**2. History updates via classmethod** (`session.py:243`)\n- `_get_new_history` is now decorated `@classmethod` (first arg `cls`), so it's callable as `RealtimeSession._get_new_history(...)` — which is exactly how the transcription-completed branch now calls it.\n- The transcription-completed branch still merges the transcript into the matching user `input_audio` placeholder item and marks it `completed`; the generic item path still replaces an existing item by `item_id`, inserts after `previous_item_id` when that item exists, or appends at the end. (One nuance worth knowing: a transcription event with no matching placeholder item yields no history change — it only merges into existing items.)\n\n**3. `close()` simplified** (`session.py:126`) — now just sets `_closed`, removes the listener, and closes the model connection. The cancel-and-await block is gone.\n\nThe `item_updated` branch keeps calling `self._get_new_history(...)`, which still works since classmethods are reachable through the instance.\n\n## Verification\n- `ruff format --check`, `ruff check`, and `mypy` all pass on the file.\n- The 9 existing realtime tests pass.\n- A behavioral check (in `/tmp/verify_session.py`, not committed) confirms: tool start/end events queue and tool output is sent inline with exceptions propagating; history replace/insert/append/merge cases; close without task cancellation; and audio/error/history/turn events.\n- Full suite: 434 passed. The 12 failures in `tests/test_config.py`/`tests/test_openai_chatcompletions*`/`tests/test_reasoning_content.py` and 7 collection errors (`litellm`, `numpy` not installed) are pre-existing — I confirmed the same failures with the original `session.py`, and they're unrelated to realtime.\n\nOne note: I left the tests alone deliberately. This change mirrors the upstream SDK's own commit (\"Tests for realtime session\"), which pairs this exact source diff with a new `tests/realtime/test_session.py` — if you want that test coverage committed alongside, I can add it.","citations":[]}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Z.AI","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"13d715a6-efdd-4627-ab02-a32241b860a9","uuid":"4c7d537b-030e-4c1f-a845-0b74c3b36f29","timestamp":"2026-09-04T06:20:10.099Z","request_id":"gen-1788502773-E97WrdFUTMlRBKHtWAtT"}
